cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this project in research or policy work, please cite it as below."
title: "Bonds-iOS (有備而來): a third-party Taiwan citizen digital identity wallet for iOS"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Bonds.tw contributors"
  - family-names: "Mashbean"
    email: "mashbean@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bonds-tw/Bonds-iOS"
url: "https://pro.mashbean.net/?series=ready-digital-government"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - digital-identity
  - digital-wallet
  - verifiable-credentials
  - openid4vci
  - openid4vp
  - sd-jwt
  - zero-knowledge
  - taiwan
  - ios
abstract: >-
  An open-source iOS wallet that holds Taiwan's national identity, government
  credentials from the official TWDIW wallet ecosystem, MyData files, and
  official electronic documents, and can present or verify them online,
  offline, and with zero-knowledge proofs. Built as a working prototype to
  test what an ideal citizen wallet should look like, with field reports
  published alongside the code.
